            <ArticleTitle>Popliteal artery aneurysm treated with implantation of a covered stent graft (fluency(®)) reinforced with a nitinol stent (S.M.A.R.T. (®)).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>316-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s12928-015-0360-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 60-year-old man was admitted for right knee pain provoked by an enlarging popliteal artery aneurysm (PAA) after endovascular therapy for thromboembolism in the right popliteal artery. The PAA was treated with implantation of a covered stent graft (Fluency(®)); however, acute thromboembolism occurred 6 months after the intervention. Therefore, we implanted a nitinol stent (S.M.A.R.T.(®)) in the proximal part of the covered stent where the major hinge point existed in addition to a stent fracture. No vascular event occurred during 4.5 years of follow-up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
